1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,363
HERO helps Virginia residents find a clearer next step after a disaster.

2
00:00:04,363 --> 00:00:12,363
A resident may know what they need, but still face uncertainty about what
to do first and what to ask a helper.

3
00:00:12,363 --> 00:00:15,999
This walkthrough uses fictional information and actual local browser
captures.

4
00:00:15,999 --> 00:00:22,180
HERO provides a curated recovery plan, optional AI explanation, and a
reviewed summary that the resident controls.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,100
The guest journey starts with three short questions.

6
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:38,138
First, HERO checks for immediate danger and directs emergencies to nine one
one.

7
00:00:38,138 --> 00:00:43,951
Next, the resident selects a current Virginia county or independent city,
or skips that question.

8
00:00:43,951 --> 00:00:45,888
Finally, they choose a need.

9
00:00:45,888 --> 00:00:48,988
A deterministic plan appears before the AI reply.

10
00:00:48,988 --> 00:00:54,801
Housing, supplies, property damage, in person assistance, and an uncertain
need each have different tasks.

11
00:00:54,801 --> 00:01:00,226
In this fictional property damage example, the resident has reviewed the
official application route.

12
00:01:00,226 --> 00:01:04,877
The next incomplete action is now prominent: confirm where the damage
occurred.

13
00:01:04,877 --> 00:01:08,752
Current locality, saved home locality, and damage locality are separate.

14
00:01:08,752 --> 00:01:14,952
Each action explains why it was selected and includes an approved federal
destination and review date.

15
00:01:14,952 --> 00:01:20,377
Completion means the resident marked a step; it does not confirm an agency
action.

16
00:01:20,377 --> 00:01:26,190
Progress survives refresh in the same tab and resets when the intake or
account changes.

17
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:34,162
This captured response came from the configured Microsoft Foundry agent.

18
00:01:34,162 --> 00:01:40,822
It explains why the location of damage matters, using an action already in
the recovery plan.

19
00:01:40,822 --> 00:01:45,400
The server supplies approved candidate actions and validated resident
reported completion.

20
00:01:45,400 --> 00:01:51,228
The model must return a short reply and up to three known action
identifiers.

21
00:01:51,228 --> 00:01:55,806
HERO rejects malformed output, unknown actions, excessive text, and
prohibited links.

22
00:01:55,806 --> 00:01:59,968
It renders action titles and destinations from its own catalog.

23
00:01:59,968 --> 00:02:04,547
The interface only says AI reply received after a successful response.

24
00:02:04,547 --> 00:02:11,206
Foundry cannot check the nearest recovery center, determine eligibility,
submit an application, or mark tasks complete.

25
00:02:11,206 --> 00:02:14,120
Invalid output leaves the resident plan available.

26
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:19,027
The resident can prepare a summary without relying on AI.

27
00:02:19,027 --> 00:02:27,485
The review includes their stated need, current locality, explicitly
selected damage locality, completed and remaining actions, approved links,
language, and date.

28
00:02:27,485 --> 00:02:33,123
They can add unresolved questions and edit the exact text that will be
exported.

29
00:02:33,123 --> 00:02:38,359
Saved home locality and household size are included only after separate
selection here.

30
00:02:38,359 --> 00:02:43,192
Saved health, disability, and support answers, and the chat history, are
excluded.

31
00:02:43,192 --> 00:02:48,024
Summary edits stay in page memory and are never sent to Foundry.

32
00:02:48,024 --> 00:02:52,454
Printing, text download, and a copy fallback support a portable handoff.

33
00:02:52,454 --> 00:02:57,690
Exporting does not contact a helper, reserve assistance, or create a case
record.

34
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:02,744
HERO also retains the existing preparedness journey.

35
00:03:02,744 --> 00:03:08,625
This fictional household has selected children and a need to plan for
powered medical equipment.

36
00:03:08,625 --> 00:03:15,290
Local rules add relevant preparation tasks, including discussing backup
arrangements with a care team or equipment provider.

37
00:03:15,290 --> 00:03:21,171
Those saved support answers do not enter the AI request or the recovery
helper summary.

38
00:03:21,171 --> 00:03:24,700
Preparedness completion is stored with the encrypted local profile.

39
00:03:24,700 --> 00:03:27,836
Recovery progress remains separate in the current tab.

40
00:03:27,836 --> 00:03:32,149
Accounts are optional, and saved profiles stay on the host computer.

41
00:03:32,149 --> 00:03:34,501
Residents should keep exported copies private.

42
00:03:34,501 --> 00:03:41,950
Encryption protects stored payloads, while access to both the database and
its key remains an important host security boundary.

43
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:50,514
English and Spanish cover the intake, recovery actions, explanations, and
export boilerplate.

44
00:03:50,514 --> 00:03:56,487
The catalog preserves the same action identifiers and approved destinations
in both languages.

45
00:03:56,487 --> 00:03:59,704
Resident written questions are not silently translated.

46
00:03:59,704 --> 00:04:02,920
Professional Spanish review remains a release check.

47
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:10,093
Here the isolated demo server was stopped and the public guide still
loaded.

48
00:04:10,093 --> 00:04:13,227
The notice explains which services require a connection.

49
00:04:13,227 --> 00:04:18,320
Accounts, saved profiles, chat, and FEMA responses are excluded from the
public cache.

50
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:24,470
This is a controlled failure demonstration with the AI provider
deliberately unconfigured.

51
00:04:24,470 --> 00:04:27,823
It is not a claim of an Azure outage.

52
00:04:27,823 --> 00:04:34,528
The status says AI unavailable, while the food and supplies plan, helper
review, and export controls remain usable.

53
00:04:34,528 --> 00:04:38,625
The resident can continue working from curated guidance and approved
destinations.

54
00:04:38,625 --> 00:04:42,350
No model response is needed to obtain a meaningful plan.

55
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:47,437
All forty four automated tests pass.

56
00:04:47,437 --> 00:04:50,686
The final English and Spanish live checks succeeded.

57
00:04:50,686 --> 00:04:53,934
These are synthetic observations, with no human participants.

58
00:04:53,934 --> 00:04:59,620
HERO provides guidance and a portable summary; it does not guarantee
assistance or outcomes.
